{"step_index":1046,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-25T13:41:40Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-25T19:11:40+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-10-25T19:11:40+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/explainer.js`\nTotal Lines: 1452\nTotal Bytes: 72015\nShowing lines 670 to 850\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n670:       // Substep 6: Explain that the result is stored back in c\n671:       const afterNum = Number(afterVal);\n672:       const ansRow = (step.variables || []).find((v) => v.name === \"ans\");\n673:       const ansNum = ansRow ? Number(ansRow.current) : null;\n674:       let whyNote = `The variable \\`${target}\\` now holds the new running sum for future comparisons and additions.`;\n675:       if (afterNum < 0) {\n676:         whyNote += ` Because \\`${afterVal}\\` is negative, the next condition (\\`if c < 0:\\`) will reset it to zero.`;\n677:       } else if (ansNum !== null && afterNum >= ansNum) {\n678:         whyNote += ` Because \\`${afterVal}\\` beats or matches \\`ans\\` (\\`${ansNum}\\`), the next condition will update \\`ans\\`!`;\n679:       }\n680: \n681:       addSubstep({\n682:         substepLabel: `Store result back in ${target}`,\n683:         codeSnippet: `${target} = ${afterVal}`,\n684:         varsBeforeStep: false,\n685:         whatIsHappening: `Python binds variable \\`${target}\\` to the new value **\\`${afterVal}\\`**. Variable \\`${target}\\` is now officially **\\`${afterVal}\\`**!`,\n686:         symbolsMeaning: `\\`+=\\` is the augmented assignment operator: it adds the right-hand value and updates the left-hand variable in one step.`,\n687:         currentValues: `${target} = ${afterVal}`,\n688:         calculationCard: {\n689:  